DevOps Implementation for Spring Boot Immunization Tracker Project
DevOps Components Added to the Spring Boot Application
In your Immunization Tracker project, you've implemented several key DevOps practices and tools to automate the build, test, deployment, and infrastructure management processes. Here's what you've done and why:

1. Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) Pipeline
Tool Used: Jenkins

Implementation: Created a Jenkins pipeline that automates the entire software delivery process

Why: To ensure consistent, repeatable builds and deployments while reducing human error

2. Containerization
Tool Used: Docker

Implementation:

Created Docker images for your Spring Boot application

Automated image building in the CI/CD pipeline

Why: To package the application with all its dependencies for consistent execution across environments

3. Container Orchestration
Tool Used: Kubernetes (via Minikube for local development)

Implementation:

Created Kubernetes manifests for deployment (deployment.yaml, service.yaml)

